Here’s how to solve the classic Two Sum problem in Python:
✅ Optimal Solution (Hash Map — best for interviews)
Python
def two_sum(nums, target):
    seen = {}  # value -> index
    
    for i, num in enumerate(nums):
        complement = target - num
        
        if complement in seen:
            return [seen[complement], i]
        
        seen[num] = i

# Example
nums = [2, 7, 11, 15]
target = 9
print(two_sum(nums, target))  # [0, 1]
💡 How it works
For each number, compute target - num
Check if that value was seen before
If yes → you found the pair
If not → store current number in the dictionary
⏱ Complexity
Time: O(n)
Space: O(n)
❌ Brute Force (for understanding)
Python
def two_sum(nums, target):
    for i in range(len(nums)):
        for j in range(i + 1, len(nums)):
            if nums[i] + nums[j] == target:
                return [i, j]
Time: O(n²) (not preferred in interviews)
